{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 105, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a 3x3 conv where edge 3 was empty gives much larger gains than replacing an existing op (exps 1,5,7,8 vs 2-4)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Creating a direct input-output path is far more valuable when none existed (exps 71,75,77,80 vs 72-74,76)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the strongest op on edge 3 with a parameter-free skip loses capacity (exps 73,78 negative vs positive otherwise)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv on edge 0 costs far more than removing a 1x1, skip, or pool (exps 22,30 vs 21,23,24)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv on node2->node3 consistently hurts more than deleting skip/1x1 (exps 62,65-70 vs 61,63)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on edge 4 with skip loses substantial accuracy, unlike replacing other ops (exps 43,50 vs 41,42)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Downgrading 3x3 to 1x1 on edge 1 is clearly harmful while replacing none/skip is neutral or positive (exp 54 vs 51,52)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv for pooling on edge 2 is negative while replacing weaker ops is neutral-to-positive (exps 34,39 vs 31-33)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "n